# Gap-lane / autoteach window — Bonsai 256 v5 (minted 2026-08-18).
#
# v4 was fully consumed: the lane took it 197 -> 0 overnight (units 703 -> 901)
# and autoteach then logged "window_exhausted". This is genuine exhaustion, not
# the stale-pointer starvation that v4 was minted to fix.
#
# Same recipe as v4: 256 ids from tools/gen_window_candidates (16735 qualifying
# word tokens), highest-ranked first, excluding ledger-closed ids (gaps.txt
# status=2, the rule bin/gap_inject applies), inbox-pending ids, and every id in
# v1/v2/v3/v4. Verified: gap_inject --dry-run reports remaining=252 of 256, the
# words file aligns 1:1 and parses under cnet_record_words_load (which refuses
# the whole file on a single malformed line).
#
# Window-only by design: this file does NOT pin CNET_TEACHER_HTTP. The teacher
# endpoint (:8081 GPU) is set independently by the zz-teacher-8081 drop-in and
# must not ride along with a window swap.
CNET_WINDOW_FILE=/home/marble/AI/CNET/english_window_256_bonsai_v5.txt
CNET_RESIDUAL_WINDOW=/home/marble/AI/CNET/english_window_256_bonsai_v5.txt
